# Cloudflare's static-assets layer reads this file natively (Workers
# static assets headers, matching the syntax Pages used) and applies
# it to every response it serves - which is most of them, since
# server/wrangler.toml's run_worker_first only sends API-shaped paths
# to worker.js and everything else is answered here without the
# Worker ever running (0.9-M1-S3, #329).
#
# This is the response-header half of the posture DESIGN.md names in
# "The constraint that shapes everything" - "The production origin is
# noindexed and sends no-referrer" - kept as a SEPARATE layer from the
# <meta name="robots"> and <meta name="referrer"> tags every page in
# this directory already carries in its own <head>: a header is read
# before a crawler or a browser parses any HTML at all, where the meta
# tags cannot reach. Neither layer replaces the other and this file
# does not touch the meta tags - see AGENTS.md, "Boundaries", on
# apps/web/ being the site as shipped rather than a place to loosen
# what a page has already declared.
#
# tools/build_web.mjs copies this file into dist/ byte for byte (no
# recognized extension, so it falls to the "copy" default) - no build
# step change needed for it to ship.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
